    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a challenging subject for me, but I appreciate its logical structure. While it wasn't my strongest point in school, I find beauty in patterns and problem-solving. My lower secondary education didn't delve deeply into advanced math, so I approach it with curiosity rather than anxiety.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "I do feel a bit anxious when faced with complex mathematical problems, especially those involving abstract concepts like calculus or statistics. However, I’ve learned to break them down step by step, which helps me manage my nerves. It’s more about patience than innate ability for me.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I haven’t used AI tools specifically for math learning yet, but I’m open to exploring them. My self-employed work doesn’t require advanced math, so my focus has been on practical skills like chemistry and history. Still, I’d be curious to see how AI could simplify or make math more engaging.",
